proposed_statement_changes.proposed:
There are universal constants \(0<c<C<\infty\) such that, for every admissible degree sequence,
\[
\Pr\!\left\{
c\,\frac{d_n^2}{n\log(d_n+1)}
\le R(G_n)\le
C\,\frac{d_n^2}{n}
\right\}\longrightarrow1.
\]
The upper inequality is attained by the one-shot graph-measurable retuned seed procedure with its branch-safe all-treated fallback, while the lower inequality ranges over every graph-dependent assignment distribution and every measurable estimator.  Thus the previously polynomial factor-\(d_n\) random-regular bracket is reduced to a logarithmic factor; no matched order or strict improvement of the \(d_n^2/n\) upper scale is asserted.

